be in charge of the Senate.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.150
- Can we pretend like we're
still before the election

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there still is the
possibility of a red wave?

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.421
- Did not work out that way.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.655
How you feeling?

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.590
- You know, with
my race, very good.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.292 align:start size:97% position:3%
We got the highest
percentage we've ever gotten.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.094
I got about 62%.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.695
In most of our rural counties,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.764
we got between 70 and 80%.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.899
We had 10 counties,

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.801
we got more than
85% of the vote,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.903
10 counties more than 80%,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:84% position:16%
probably all together,
about 50 counties,

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.506
more than 70% of the vote.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.242 align:start size:81% position:19%
So that kind of
shows a little bit

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.544
