side of the Potomac River

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.522
are very Democrat,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
but they're all federal
government workers.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you grow the
federal government,

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:48.194
you make it harder for a
Republican to win Virginia.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Is that your
biggest frustration,

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.398 align:start position:0%
as probably the most libertarian
senator that we have,

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.667
that people just, in
the end of the day,

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
despite candidate
quality or anything else,

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.973
they kinda just want
more stuff, sadly?

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.242
- Well, it is, and I
talk about it a lot.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, when I talk to folks
at home around the country,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.614
it's that what we're
offering is intangible.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.182
We're offering the opportunity,

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.550
